\textbf{Reasoning:}
Let the initial number of people on the train be $P_0 = 172$.
At the first stop, 47 people get off, so the number of people on the train becomes $P_1 = P_0 - 47 = 172 - 47 = 125$.
Then, 13 people get on, so the number of people on the train becomes $P_2 = P_1 + 13 = 125 + 13 = 138$.
At the next stop, 38 people get off, so the number of people on the train becomes $P_3 = P_2 - 38 = 138 - 38 = 100$.
Therefore, the number of people on the train is 100.

\textbf{Final Answer:}
\boxed{100}

